[{"id":123364,"sender_id":1024,"sender_full_name":"Samuel Adrian Antz","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3cf65b33b707c0ede6bb3bfa7f4670cf?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/General.20questions/near/123364\">#1</a> I’ve created this discussion to ask a few general questions about editing the nLab, which don’t fit into my previous discussion <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/Title.20convention/with/116040\">title convention</a>. A few have gathered in the past weeks. My first one is about which convention to use for articles about <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/general%20relativity\">general relativity</a> as I have a few new in preparation. Is the mathematical convention (for example <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Ric}-\\frac{R}{2}g+\\Lambda g=\\kappa T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Ric</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2173em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8723em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Λ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span>) prefered or the physical convention (for example <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\mu\\nu}-\\frac{R}{2}g_{\\mu\\nu}+\\Lambda g_{\\mu\\nu}=\\kappa T_{\\mu\\nu}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0077em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0637em;\">μν</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2173em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8723em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0637em;\">μν</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Λ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0637em;\">μν</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">κ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0637em;\">μν</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>)? Or using both with a remark at the beginning?</p>","timestamp":1767708073,"subject":"General questions","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":123368,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/General.20questions/near/123368\">#2</a> It’s generally unfeasible to impose and hence to rely on conventions across different nLab entries. Not only is it already extrmely hard to agree on a convention among people currently active, but there is no way to guarantee that any future editor sticks to any given set of conventions or will even be aware of them.</p>\n<p>Therefore, where it matters, each entry needs to establish its own conventions.</p>\n<p>This is not as bad as it sounds. If you have a section on some page that establishes some set of conventions, then every other page can just point to that, saying “we use conventions as listed there”.</p>\n<p>On the other hand, in your special case of tensor notation it is not clear that you even want to fix a convention: Both notations you list have their use in given circumstances.</p>","timestamp":1767724572,"subject":"General questions","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":124090,"sender_id":1024,"sender_full_name":"Samuel Adrian Antz","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3cf65b33b707c0ede6bb3bfa7f4670cf?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/General.20questions/near/124090\">#3</a> Here the question mentioned yesterday in the discussions for <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/spin%20bordism\">spin bordism</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/spin%E1%B6%9C%20bordism\">spinᶜ bordism</a> and <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/spin%CA%B0%20bordism\">spinʰ bordism</a>. I couldn’t post it then due to some odd gateway error. The paper has three tables for the repsective bordism groups up to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\leq 99</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">99</span></span></span></span>. What and how should that be added into the articles? Everything in a list, maybe with a cutoff or as a table like in the paper?</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Jonathan%20Buchanan\">Jonathan Buchanan</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Stephen%20McKean\">Stephen McKean</a>: <em>KSp-characteristic classes determine Spin cobordism</em>, Algebr. Geom. Topol. <strong>26</strong> (2026) 485-551 [<a href=\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2312.08209\">arXiv:2312.08209</a>, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2026.26.485\">doi:10.2140/agt.2026.26.485</a>]</li>\n</ul>","timestamp":1773821082,"subject":"General questions","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":124093,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/General.20questions/near/124093\">#4</a> As you like. You could also upload png scans of their tables, as I have now done <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/spin+bordism#TableOfSpinCobordismGroups\">here</a>.</p>","timestamp":1773824967,"subject":"General questions","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]